This is very strange. Let me wonder if maybe there's a character limit issue. Or I need to use a specific XML version.

OK let me consider doing this from yet another angle. The string ref works, so let me write with STRING reference (the spec mentions "anyOf" with string option). But not all formats may support this. Let me check write schema.

Write tool: 
```
"entity_ref": {
  "anyOf": [
    {"additionalProperties": {}, "type": "object"},
    {"type": "string"}
  ]
}
```

So entity_ref can be string!

Still empty `{}`. OK the XML content is being parsed by the harness as `{}` always. There's something wrong.

Let me think. Look at this: `<content>{}</content>` — the harness is sometimes confused with my own content like `{"method": "POST"}` because it has nested `{}`. Maybe the harness parses `{}` as an empty JSON?

Wait — look closely: the content is currently being persisted as EXACTLY `{}`, not even `{"method": null}` or similar. So my entire content gets cleared.

OK let me try a brand new approach — use edit on a created request entity, passing entity_ref as just a string (since edit clearly says object only in some cases). Actually let me check edit schema:

```
